I have been *thinking* about attempting a Finnish version.  The problem
is that my C skills are far too low for me to be able to construct cases
(all 15 of them) correctly; this would require many tables of word
stems.  Also, I couldn't do functions to append case suffixes to words.

I *did* translate the monsters and objects but got stuck with objnam.c,
which would be required to redo for correct naming of the objects.  I
used the Spanish NetHack as a foundation since that way I could get
characters right even in ms-dos/DJGPP (I haven't tried MinGW).  Using
the Spanish versions created more problems as I don't know Spanish well,
and the word order in Finnish is often closer to English than Spanish...

The Finnish project was very private and I haven't been considering it
for months now.

